{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.687,
   "text": "The Marlowe twins had a dollhouse built just like their real house... down to the tiniest chair."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.287,
   "end": 14.553,
   "text": "Their mom gave me one rule the night I started babysitting."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.153,
   "end": 19.356,
   "text": "Never move the dolls. Whatever they're doing... leave them be."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.156,
   "end": 24.7,
   "text": "There were four. A mother, a father... and two little girls in their beds."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.3,
   "end": 31.081,
   "text": "My second week, a fifth doll showed up. A girl with a brown ponytail... just like mine."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 31.781,
   "end": 37.648,
   "text": "Every night, she was somewhere new. The kitchen. The hallway. A little closer to the twins' room."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.348,
   "end": 43.063,
   "text": "Then one Friday, near midnight, I heard a tiny click from the playroom."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.263,
   "end": 49.895,
   "text": "The ponytail doll stood at the top of the dollhouse stairs... facing the twins' door."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.795,
   "end": 54.976,
   "text": "I broke the rule. I pulled her out, and shoved her in my pocket."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 55.676,
   "end": 58.108,
   "text": "The house went very quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.708,
   "end": 64.039,
   "text": "Then, upstairs... the real stairs creaked. One step at a time."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.239,
   "end": 71.444,
   "text": "When Mrs. Marlowe got home, she saw the empty dollhouse stairs... and went white."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.144,
   "end": 76.688,
   "text": "That doll was you, she whispered. She keeps something off those stairs."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 77.688,
   "end": 80.504,
   "text": "So what did you just let climb them?"
  }
 ],
